  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Making Universal Basic Education more inclusive to children with disabilities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Nigeria, despite the introduction of universal education (UBE), very few children with disabilities attend primary or junior secondary schools. This was especially noted by Nigerian Diaspora volunteers who took part in a teaching programme in Ipaja, Lagos State, in 2011. This research project will enable Ipaja Community Link (ICL) staff to work with the local government council to indentify children with disabilities who live in and around Ipaja. It will then ascertain the training needed for teachers to start adequate inclusive education in schools, with one school used as a pilot to test and develop good practice. Civil society groups which can assist in the project will be approached and coordinated. The outcome will be increased uptake of Universal Basic Education (UBE) in Ipaja by children with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
